\title{kolibri: Kernel-Operations for Long-read Insertion, Breakpoint and Recombination Inspection}
\description{
\if{html}{\figure{logo.png}{options: style='float: right' alt='logo' width='120'}}

Tools for inspecting long-read alignments (PacBio/ONT) exported as BED12 to find, group, and visualize split reads. Split reads—reads that map to two or more genomic locations—are indicators of structural variation, transposable element insertions, recombination breakpoints, and assembly errors. kolibri clusters these split segments per chromosome using sweep, DBSCAN, or kernel-density-based algorithms, builds a shared-read network connecting related clusters, and provides a suite of visualization functions for exploring the network and individual nodes.
